*** Add File:ops/grpc/README.md
+# Aegis gRPC services
+
+This folder contains:
+- .proto files: ops/proto/*.proto
+- Servers: ops/grpc/*_server.py
+- Clients: ops/grpc/*_client.py
+- A helper to generate Python stubs: ops/grpc/_generate_stubs.py
+
+Quick start (local)
+1. Install deps:
+   pip install -r ops/grpc/requirements.txt
+2. Generate stubs:
+   python3 ops/grpc/_generate_stubs.py
+3. Start services (each in its own terminal):
+   python3 ops/grpc/evidence_server.py
+   python3 ops/grpc/dp_server.py
+   python3 ops/grpc/serve_server.py
+4. Use clients:
+   python3 ops/grpc/evidence_client.py
+   python3 ops/grpc/dp_client.py
+   python3 ops/grpc/serve_client.py
+
+Security note: running gRPC servers here uses insecure channels for simplicity. In production you should:
+- Use mTLS (create server credentials and call grpc.secure_channel with credentials),
+- Use Kubernetes secrets for TLS certs and configure servers to load them,
+- Enforce network policies and mutual TLS in your mesh.
+
